+# Speculative Decoding Deployment Guide (staging)
+
+1) Build & push images
+
+ - student:
+     cd services/speculative/student
+     docker build -t us.gcr.io/aegis/student-stub:latest .
+     docker push us.gcr.io/aegis/student-stub:latest
+
+ - teacher:
+     cd services/speculative/teacher
+     docker build -t us.gcr.io/aegis/teacher-stub:latest .
+     docker push us.gcr.io/aegis/teacher-stub:latest
+
+ - orchestrator & proxy:
+     Build images for services/speculative/orchestrator.py and services/serving/speculative_proxy.py (these were added earlier in the repo).
+     Tag as us.gcr.io/aegis/spec-orchestrator:latest and us.gcr.io/aegis/spec-proxy:latest and push.
+
+2) Deploy to cluster (namespace 'inference' assumed)
+
+ kubectl create ns inference --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
+ kubectl apply -f k8s/speculative/student-deployment.yaml
+ kubectl apply -f k8s/speculative/teacher-deployment.yaml
+ kubectl apply -f k8s/speculative/orchestrator-deployment.yaml
+ kubectl apply -f k8s/speculative/proxy-deployment.yaml
+
+3) Prometheus & Grafana
+
+ - Apply prometheus scrape config:
+     kubectl apply -f monitoring/prometheus/speculative-scrape-config.yaml
+
+ - Import Grafana dashboard (monitoring/grafana/speculative_dashboard.json) using ops/grafana/import_dashboard.sh
+
+4) Pilot
+
+ - Start in shadow mode: route traffic to spec-proxy but have your frontend ignore speculative outputs; alternatively call spec-orchestrator with a shadow flag (not present in stub; use proxy routing config).
+ - Run locust: use ops/tests/locust_speculative_locustfile.py to generate load.
+ - Inspect metrics in Grafana and logs at /var/log/aegis/speculative_events.jsonl (inside orchestrator pods).
+
+Notes:
+ - Replace stub student/teacher with your model endpoints and ensure tokenization parity before accepting production traffic.
+ - Tune SPEC_ACCEPT_THRESHOLD, SPEC_CHUNK_LEN and SPEC_BATCH_INTERVAL_MS based on shadow metrics.
+
